    "catalog:format": "2",
    "catalog:tags": "wc, toilet, close-coupled, bathroom",
    "catalog:note": "Close-coupled WC against the wall, lid open. seat 0.42, rim 0.40. The pan is an oval outline sweep, hollowed by a shell 0.015 thick whose top is opened by a round bowl cut, on an oval pedestal that follows the pan. The seat is two half rings that meet on the centre line. Cistern on the rear of the pan with a push button on top; the button, radius 0.02, is drawn at true size.",
    "catalog:basedOn": "Drafting standard key dimensions (practice, Neufert / Metric Handbook), unverified: WC 0.37 x 0.65 x 0.78, seat 0.42; EN 997 not read. Pan oval, pedestal and bowl opening are generic shapes, unverified. Port sizes from the drafting standard (BS EN 12056-2 conventions), unverified",
    "ifc:class": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
    "ifc:predefinedType": "TOILETPAN",
    "ifcClass": "IfcSanitaryTerminal",
